---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BmiCalculator from '../../../components/BmiCalculator.astro';
import Faq from '../../../components/Faq.astro';

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'BMI Calculator',
    url: 'https://tdeecheck.com/calculators/bmi-calculator/',
    applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is a healthy BMI?',
    a: 'For most adults, a BMI between 18.5 and 24.9 is classed as the healthy range. It is a population screening range, not a personal verdict. Athletes, older adults, and some ethnic groups can be healthy outside it, which is why context matters.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does BMI say I am overweight when I lift weights?',
    a: 'BMI only uses height and weight, so it cannot tell muscle from fat. A muscular person can land in the overweight band with low body fat and excellent health markers. Waist measurement and body composition give a fuller picture.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is BMI used for children?',
    a: 'Not in this form. Children and teens are assessed with BMI percentiles that account for age and sex, because they are still growing. This calculator is for adults only.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I lower my BMI safely?',
    a: 'The same way you lower weight safely: a modest calorie deficit of 250 to 500 kcal below your TDEE, high protein, regular activity, and patience. About 0.5 to 1 lb per week is a realistic, sustainable rate for most people.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BMI Calculator - Body Mass Index and Healthy Weight Range"
  description="Free BMI calculator for adults. Get your Body Mass Index, its category, a visual gauge, and the healthy weight range for your height."
  path="/calculators/bmi-calculator/"
  schemas={schemas}
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Calculators', path: '/calculators/' },
    { name: 'BMI Calculator', path: '/calculators/bmi-calculator/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900">BMI Calculator</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
        Body Mass Index is a quick screening number based on your height and weight. Calculate yours, see where it sits,
        and get the healthy weight range for your height.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-4xl">
      <BmiCalculator />
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-14">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">How BMI is calculated</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      The formula is simple: weight in kilograms divided by height in meters squared. The categories used worldwide for
      adults are underweight below 18.5, healthy from 18.5 to 24.9, overweight from 25 to 29.9, and the obesity range at
      30 and above. BMI survives in clinics and research because it is fast, free, and correlates reasonably well with
      health risk across large populations.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">What BMI does not tell you</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      BMI cannot see composition. It does not know whether your weight is muscle, fat, bone, or water, and it does not know
      where fat is stored, even though waist fat carries more risk than hip fat. Treat a surprising BMI as a prompt for a
      better check, not a conclusion. Waist circumference, blood pressure, blood markers, fitness, and how you feel all
      belong in the picture. Pair your BMI with your calorie numbers from the
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/">TDEE Calculator</a> and you have a workable starting point
      either way.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Turning a BMI result into a plan</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      If your BMI sits above the healthy range and the result rings true, the healthy weight range on this page shows a
      realistic first destination: the top of the range, not the bottom. Reaching it at 0.5 to 1 lb per week is a genuine
      health win. If your BMI is below range, a gradual surplus and a check in with a clinician are the right next steps.
      Sudden or unexplained weight change in either direction always deserves a medical look.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 rounded-xl bg-brand-50 border border-brand-100 px-5 py-4 text-sm text-ink-700">
      Reviewed by <strong>Farah Akram, Dietitian</strong>. BMI is a screening estimate, not a diagnosis. See the
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/medical-disclaimer/">medical disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <Faq faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
